WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.500
 [silence]

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.500
 Hey! Hey!

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.800
 [silence]

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.500
 Hey! Hey!

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.500
 We don't need your nagging cover

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.500
 We're too poor, shy of superstardom

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.500
 No glossy photos, no billboard chart

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.000
 Sleeping on couches, playing basements

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.500
 Free minds won't bow to a corporate arch

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.500
 They want us clean-shaven, posing pretty

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.000
 Selling our souls for a ten-year plan

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.500
 But we'd better stink of cheap PBR

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.500
 Then sell our songs to a greased-up man

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.500
 Why isn't our souls for a flashy tour?

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.500
 No, we'll leave that ship at the dock

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.500
 Your velvet ropes and VIP rooms get f*cked right off

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.000
 Still not famous, still not sorry

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.500
 Rather bleed truth and borrow their story

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.000
 Yo, A&R telling us what to play

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
 We write our own rules and sing our own way

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.500
 Still not famous, still not sorry

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.000
 Rap too proud for sorry-story

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.500
 Keep it in a gorge, crank it 'til it bleeds

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.500
 Freedom's our drug, face just a disease

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.000
 They promise exposure, a million streams

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.500
 But it's just state of mind in your teenage dreams

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.500
 We're fine with free fans in a sweaty room

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.000
 Trading our fame for creative perfume

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.500
 No neon signs, no corporate bailout

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.000
 We live for the core changes in our veins

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
 If the scene goes sideways, we'll still stay true

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.500
 'Cause selling us the only thing that's lame

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.000
 Call track for gold bars and grand illusions

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.500
 We laugh so hard we almost pissed

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.500
 We're allergic to mansions and red-guitar solos

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.000
 Give us scrappy real, not famous, still not sorry

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.500
 Rather bleed truth and borrow their story

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.500
 No, A&R telling us what to play

